  "worked_solution": "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={21}^{\u2218}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-21).\n$$",
